    "language_authority": "The Wright native process language is the semantic authority for AI/programmatic clients, canvas, readable text and runtime. Autonomous AI authoring and Rivet migration/retirement remain separate work.",
    "capabilities": [
      "In the local feature build, create/configure/connect/save/reopen native processes with exact typed ports and one official language for programmatic clients, Inspector, canvas and runtime.",
      "Run all three development examples and inspect actual artifact bytes and provenance. Browser verification includes the 135 g mass result, a deliberate failure and a linked correction with the old snapshot preserved.",
      "The shared HTTP CLI and native runtime support durable evidence, cancellation/recovery and exact local MCP binding. A real disposable stdio tool process produced a verified artifact and exited cleanly.",
      "This is local feature-branch delivery. Full candidate gates, human usability, dev PR/deployment and final acceptance remain pending; benchmark qualification remains 0/100."
    ],
